@aiwayds/dsh-subagent-registry README · `@deepseek-ai/*` 依赖契约（为什么是 optional peer）：维护守则：这些包永远保持 optional peer 形态——不要移回 dependencies /
devDependencies，也不要去掉 `optional: true`（非 optional peer 在
`auto-install-peers` 开启的 pnpm 下会被自动安装，第二副本问题即复发）；同样不要新增任何硬 dependencies——钉死的第二份拷贝会以同样方式遮蔽宿主闭包。

@aiwayds/dsh-subagent-registry README · The three shipped agents (the seed trio) + two opt-ins：Seeded into `~/.dsh/agents/` on first start (only when the directory holds no
parsable agent — your edits are never overwritten). All three are ordinary
markdown files: edit them freely.

@aiwayds/dsh-subagent-registry README · The ptc capability (opt-in: the codemode tool)：> ⚠️ **Experimental — disabled by default**: the capability has migrated and
> merged, the product surface stays experimental; `ptcEnabled: false` (the
> default) registers no tool.

@aiwayds/dsh-subagent-registry README · The `@deepseek-ai/*` dependency contract (why optional peers)：This repo declares the `@deepseek-ai/*` packages (`cordis`, `dsh-subagent`,
`dsh-llm`, `schemastery`, …) as **optional peerDependencies** in releases
(`>=0.2.0-rc.2 || >=0.2.1-rc.1`). That is a deliberate two-layer split:
